}

3.7 Model-adjusted EPP across the phylogeny
The pruned phylogeny was used to visualise model-adjusted species-level EPP frequencies. These are partially pooled posterior estimates from the overall beta-binomial model, not raw species proportions. The plotted estimate retains the phylogenetic and non-phylogenetic species effects while fixing the population random effect at zero.


